 fiscal discipline, achieving a budget execution rate exceeding 80.0% [Data: Entities (5)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Strategic Execution and Dependency of Project P-01 and Project P-02\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Project P-01 is a strategic cloud-native migration initiative responsible for deploying Kubernetes (K8s) networking infrastructure, operating under an approved budget of 350 million KRW authorized by Park Young-hee [Data: Entities (24, 167); Relationships (434)]. Kim Chul-soo serves as the General Project Manager (PM), with key contributions from Senior Engineer Lee Seon-im (also referenced as Lee Seonim) [Data: Entities (8, 10, 23); Relationships (10, 34)].\\n\\nProject P-02, an initiative focused on building an enterprise-grade Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) platform, directly depends on the Kubernetes network infrastructure delivered by Project P-01 [Data: Entities (24, 25); Relationships (161)]. Choi Chaek-im, a lead engineer dispatched from the Cloud Operations Team, acts as core personnel and senior architect for P-02 to secure its operational and technical viability [Data: Entities (9, 126); Relationships (8, 303)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Architecture Review Board Governance and Technical Standards\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Enterprise technical standardization is governed by the Enterprise Architecture Review Board (ARB) [Data: Entities (75); Relationships (173)]. On February 18, 2026, the ARB-2026-Q1-04 meeting addressed critical standards for Enterprise Agentic RAG and vLLM model serving [Data: Entities (78); Relationships (173)].\\n\\nThe session included key participants from multiple divisions. Principal Hong Timjang, leader of the AI Team within the AI Innovation Division, co-presented proposals for hybrid search and context preservation chunking standards alongside Choi Chaek-im [Data: Entities (9, 73, 76); Relationships (175, 203)]. Additionally, Yun Agent, PM of Project P-04 (AI Security Guardrails), attended to coordinate security and Human-In-The-Loop (HITL) compliance [Data: Entities (77); Relationships (183)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Incident Response and Hybrid Infrastructure Remediation\",\n      \"explanation\": \"On February 9, 2026, the organization experienced Incident PM-2026-001, a Sev-2 severity disruption that lasted 87 minutes [Data: Entities (85)]. The incident involved KV cache out-of-memory (OOM) errors and connection pool exhaustion across hybrid Kubernetes cluster nodes spanning Pangyo and Seoul [Data: Entities (84, 85); Relationships (214)].\\n\\nOperational resolution required coordinated inter-departmental efforts. Kim Chul-soo actively commanded response operations, supported by critical remediation actions from Choi Chaek-im and engineer Cho En-ji to restore cluster stability [Data: Entities (8, 9, 86); Relationships (213)]. Choi Chaek-im subsequently introduced a database read-only proxy (PgBouncer) and a 5-second circuit breaker for Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools to prevent recurring disruptions [Data: Entities (9)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Operational Resilience via Drills and Blue-Green Cutover Rehearsals\",\n      \"explanation\": \"To safeguard systems against outages and maintain high availability, the Cloud Operations Team executes structured operational readiness routines. Regular Disaster Recovery (DR) drills are conducted in tandem with continuous 24x365 monitoring to validate multi-cloud resilience [Data: Entities (5, 11, 23); Relationships (11)].\\n\\nTo manage deployment delay risks associated with complex cloud migrations, the team also instituted Blue-Green Cutover Rehearsals [Data: Entities (127)]. Conducted twice during low-traffic nighttime windows between 02:00 and 05:00, these rehearsals were jointly executed by Senior Engineer Lee Seon-im to validate infrastructure cutover procedures under controlled conditions [Data: Entities (10, 127); Relationships (304)].\"\n    }\n  ],\n